course: dictionary
lesson: 6101
title: Mexican: where something comes from
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Mexican is a word that tells you where someone or something comes from. It can describe a thing, or it can name a person. «Frida Kahlo, a Mexican painter, was badly hurt in a bus crash as a teenager.» Here Mexican describes the painter: she comes from Mexico.
explain: When Mexican names a person, it means someone from Mexico. «Mexicans» is the plural, meaning more than one person. Check your meaning with the swap trick: if "from Mexico" fits in the place of Mexican and still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: Mexican can also describe food in the style of Mexico, such as tacos and burritos. «Let's get Mexican» means let's get Mexican food. Read the words around Mexican to decide which meaning fits: a painter, a fish, a wave, or a meal.
fact: Mexican can be an adjective: it describes something, like a Mexican painter.
fact: A Mexican is a noun: a person from Mexico, and the plural is Mexicans.
fact: Mexican food means food in the style of Mexico, such as tacos and burritos.
fact: «Mexican tetra» fish live in dark caves and have lost their eyes, because eyes are useless in total darkness.
fact: «Mexican free-tailed bats» may fly over 160 kilometres an hour, though not all scientists agree.
exercise: In «Frida Kahlo, a Mexican painter, was badly hurt in a bus crash», what kind of word is Mexican? | A verb, an action word | A noun, naming a place | A question word | *An adjective, describing the painter
exercise: What is the plural of «a Mexican», meaning more than one person from Mexico? | Mexicanly | Mexico | *Mexicans | Mexican food
exercise: «Let's get Mexican» for dinner means what? | *Food in the style of Mexico, such as tacos | A wave at the football stadium | A bus to the airport | A painting of a face
test: Which phrase is about food? | Mexican painter | Mexican wave | *Mexican food | Mexican fish
test: In «Mexican free-tailed bats may fly over a hundred and sixty kilometres an hour», what does Mexican tell you? | The bats have no wings | The bats are very sad | *The bats are from Mexico | The bats are cooked for dinner
exam: In «He is a Mexican», what kind of word is Mexican? | *A noun, naming a person from Mexico | An adjective, describing a thing | A full stop | A verb, an action word
